  Copyright (C) 2026 Kreuder <mk@singular.de>

  The icon's ground: a dark tile with the reel's disc on it, as the mark sits on the page in
  @drawable/ic_wordmark. The tile is a full-bleed rectangle so that every launcher mask — circle,
  squircle, rounded square — is filled to its own edge; the gradient is no longer the ground but
  the disc, slate-400 into slate-500, drawn where the artwork drew it.

  The disc is the circle inscribed in the adaptive icon's central 72 units, which is where
  @drawable/ic_launcher_foreground maps the mark's own disc — so the arcs still meet the edge at
  the proportion they were drawn at, and a round mask cuts along the disc's edge rather than
  through the tile.

  The ramp is pinned to where it ran in the artwork (the disc's inscribed diagonal, mapped onto
  this canvas), so the mark meets the same colours it was drawn against.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#020618"
        android:pathData="M0,0 L108,0 L108,108 L0,108 Z" />

    <path android:pathData="M54,18 A36,36 0 1,0 54,90 A36,36 0 1,0 54,18 Z">
        <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
            <gradient
                android:type="linear"
                android:startX="27.42"
                android:startY="27.75"
                android:endX="80.58"
                android:endY="79.79">
                <item android:offset="0" android:color="#90A1B9" />
                <item android:offset="1" android:color="#62748E" />
            </gradient>
        </aapt:attr>
    </path>
</vector>
